6. AI-generated content disclosure
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Orca OC concept art and variants were generated with an AI image model
(openai/gpt-image-2.6-sunburst via OpenRouter Images API) on 2026-11-14/15 and
then screened/processed by the author. Voice pilot audio was generated with the
DeepSeek TTS API (voice "stella") on 2026-11-14. Placeholder sprite packs are
generated deterministically by scripts (no image model).

AI labelling is mandatory, not optional. Under China's AI-generated content
labelling rules (effective 2025-09-01) and GB 45438-2025, AI content needs both
explicit labels (visible text/badge) and implicit labels (metadata); labels must
not be deleted, hidden or forged. Platform terms (DeepSeek platform terms, Steam
content survey for pre-generated and live AI, Apple/Google store policies where
applicable) and EU AI Act Article 50 (applicable from 2026-08-02) also apply. Do
not present AI-generated art or voice as human-made or as real recordings. The
final disclosure plan is pending legal review.

As-built status (2026-11-17, must not be overstated):
- Explicit in-app badge: one small "AI 合成·非真人" badge exists (pet.html), but
  it is 8px / ~2.17:1 contrast and not reachable by hover/keyboard — below the
  "significant label" standard.
- Implicit labels: NOT implemented. No PNG tEXt/XMP/IPTC/C2PA writer exists in
  this repository; flagged images and audio carry no machine-readable AI label.
- Audio label: no player label / spoken start prompt / earcon is implemented; the
  "AI voice · synthetic" text exists only as an unused constant.
- Export labels: NOT implemented (no export pipeline for AI audio/images).
- The TOS does not yet state the labelling method/style required by the Chinese
  labelling measures; a draft method is in docs/legal/AI-LABELING.md (DRAFT).
- Store AI declarations have not been made (no store release).
- C2PA vs XMP/tEXt/IPTC is still TBD. Do not claim "C2PA" or "metadata added".

Synthetic voice must additionally be disclosed at first use and labelled in the
player/UI ("AI voice / synthetic"), and any exported audio must carry the label.
Voice cloning of real people is prohibited without written authorisation.

Provenance records: AI-PROVENANCE.md (Orca, Pearl, TTS). Do not include API keys
in any provenance file.

